&Q000788 = A man and his god
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.5.2.4
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.5.2.4&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

@div ŋišgiŋal A

A.1. lu₂-ulu₃ nam-mah diŋir-ra-na zid-de₃-eš-še₃ he₂-em-me
#tr.en: A person should steadfastly proclaim the exaltedness of his god.
#lem: lulu[man]; nammah[greatness]; diŋir[deity]; zid[right]; e[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=A.1

#etcsl#cite Cited in OB catalogue in the Louvre, 0.2.02, line 45

A.2. ŋuruš-e inim diŋir-ra-na kug-ge-eš he₂-em-i-i
#tr.en: A young man should devoutly praise the words of his god;
#lem: ŋuruš[young adult male]; inim[word]; diŋir[deity]; kug[pure]; e[bring out]
#etcsl: line-id=A.2

A.3. kalam zid-de-a uŋ₃ dur₂-ru-na-bi gu-gin₇ ha-ba-si-il-e
#tr.en: the people living in the righteous Land should unravel them like a thread.
#lem: kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; zid[right]; uŋ[people]; durun[sit]; gu[cord]; sil[split]
#etcsl: line-id=A.3

A.4. {ŋiš}balaŋ di ušur gu₅-li-ni ur₅!(IR) hu#-mu-un-na-bur₂-e
#tr.en: May the @fsux{balaŋ} singer assuage the spirit of his neighbour and friend.
#lem: balaŋ[an instrument]; di[speak]; usar[(female) neighbor]; guli[friend]; ur[liver]; bur[spread out]
#etcsl: line-id=A.4

A.5. šag₄ X he₂-eb-huŋ-e
#tr.en: May it soothe their (?) hearts, bring forth ……,
#lem: šag[heart]; X; huŋ[pacify]
#etcsl: line-id=A.5

A.6. X [he₂-ni]-in#-e₃ [...]-bi he₂-ni-ib-be₂
#tr.en: utter ……,
#lem: X; e[leave]; X; e[speak]
#etcsl: line-id=A.6

A.7. [...] X X he₂#-aŋ₂-e
#tr.en: and measure out …….
#lem: X; X; X; aŋ[measure]
#etcsl: line-id=A.7

A.8. ka i-si-iš ŋal₂-la-ni šag₄ diŋir-ra-na he₂-em-huŋ-e
#tr.en: Let his mouth shaping a lament soothe the heart of his god,
#lem: kag[mouth]; isiš[tears]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]; šag[heart]; diŋir[deity]; huŋ[pacify]
#etcsl: line-id=A.8

A.9. lu₂-ulu₃ diŋir-da nu-me-a u₂-gu₇ la-ba-ak-e
#tr.en: for a man without a god does not obtain food.
#lem: lulu[man]; diŋir[deity]; me[be]; ugu[food]; ak[do]
#etcsl: line-id=A.9

A.10. ŋuruš-e a₂-ni ki-lul-la hul la-ba-e-ŋa₂-ŋa₂
#tr.en: There is a young man who does not wickedly put his efforts into evil murder,
#lem: ŋuruš[young adult male]; a[arm]; kilulak[murder]; hulu[bad]; ŋar[put]
#etcsl: line-id=A.10

A.11. [a]-nir# a₂-sag₃ du-lum gig-ga ud# im-ma-ni-in-zal#
#tr.en: yet he spends the time in grief, @fsux{asag} illness and bitter suffering.
#lem: anir[lament]; Asag[1]DN; dulum[toil]; gig[sick]; ud[sun]; zal[pass time]
#etcsl: line-id=A.11

A.12. [...] X RA nam-tar-e su-gu₇-e [...]-ge# mu-un-ni-ib-te
#tr.en: The fate demon has brought need and …… close to him.
#lem: X; X; X; Namtar[1]DN; sugu[need]; X; teŋ[approach]
#etcsl: line-id=A.12

A.13. [X X] gig#-ga umuš-bi mu-suh₃ X X X-na mu-un-dul
#tr.en: Bitter …… has confused his judgment (?) of it, and covered his …….
#lem: X; X; gig[sick]; umuš[consideration]; suh[confuse]; X; X; X; dul[cover]
#etcsl: line-id=A.13

A.14. a-ga-e šu hul mu-ni-ib-dug₄ X X-še₃
#tr.en: Behind his back they have overpowered him like a …….
#lem: aga[rear]; šu[hand]; hulu[bad]; dug[speak]; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=A.14

A.15. šul-e igi diŋir-ra-na
#tr.en: Before his god the youth,
#lem: šul[youth]; igi[eye]; diŋir[deity]
#etcsl: line-id=A.15

A.16. ŋuruš-e a₂ hul ŋar-ra-na er₂ gig# i₃-še₈-še₈
#tr.en: the young man weeps bitterly over the malice he has suffered.
#lem: ŋuruš[young adult male]; a[arm]; hulu[bad]; ŋar[put]; er[tears]; gig[sick]; šeš[weep]
#etcsl: line-id=A.16

